form_export/: a board interposer-pnr export --form drew against a sheet, at
interposer-pnr 0120739, and drew again byte for byte at adf9dbf. Its round_trip is
version 3, a sheet board without reserved copper, which the reader at the commit
_vendor/round_trip_names.SOURCE states still reads. They are its tests/test_sheet_form.py
carrier case with a lone sheet net (the inputs its tests/test_round_trip_names.py
reads): export_with_form(out, data, pads=CARRIER_PADS) with
data = with_carriers(form_data()) plus net(LONE, ("D_ROT", "A1")), run with
HCDP_ROOT set. The last drawing ran 07a36d2's code with tests/test_cli.py
footprint_design as interposer-pnr 3e85398 states it: the interposer declares
attachment_surface_z 10.8103 and its dies sit at z 54.8103 (the plane plus the
44 um copper pillar).
Place and route never read a die's z, so neither line moves the board or the
report; io_pads.chiplet carries both. 3e85398 is an unmerged commit, so the digests
below, not that commit, are what binds the files. draft.kicad_pcb and
io_pads.chiplet (the assembly it exported, whose io_pads are the planner's) are as
written, with the output folder taken out of the GDS_FILE paths. export.json keeps
only format, version and round_trip of the report, with the same paths shortened.
